 "result": "All in `src/tessel/views.py`:\n\n1. **`VerbView.__init_subclass__`** (line 165) runs when you define the subclass. It scans for `get`, `post`, etc. (names in `http_method_funcs`) and sets `cls.methods` to the uppercase set, e.g. `{\"GET\", \"POST\"}`.\n\n2. **`View.to_view_func()`** (line 86) is the classmethod that turns the class into a view function. It builds an inner `view(**kwargs)` closure that:\n   - creates `view.view_class(...)` per request when `init_every_request` is True (or reuses one instance otherwise);\n   - calls `active_app.ensure_sync(self.run_view)(**kwargs)`;\n   - applies any `decorators`, then copies `view_class`, `methods`, `provide_automatic_options`, `__name__`, `__doc__` and `__module__` onto the function (lines 129–134).\n\n   The route registration reads `view.methods`, so only the verbs you defined are allowed.\n\n3. **`VerbView.run_view()`** (line 181) does the per-request routing. It runs `getattr(self, request.method.lower())`, falls back to `get` for HEAD if there's no `head` handler, and calls the handler with the URL kwargs through `ensure_sync`.",
